    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8069c526_594b5971",
        "filename": "zephyr/dts/bindings/cros_flash/cros-ec,flash-layout.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-29T19:18:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like the Zephyr devicetree support doesn\u0027t populate the default properties into the final generated DTS file.  Instead, the default values are populated into the devicetree_generated.h file.\n\nSo the default values are available to the C code, but binman processes the DTS directly and won\u0027t see the default value.\n\nConsidering binman\u0027s default padding is 0, it would be confusing to setup a different default here.",
      "parentUuid": "f914a830_3053ab20",
      "revId": "8e86c7b0aa8c2afed21d9a9632b615682987d824",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7063d2c1_259603b5",
        "filename": "zephyr/dts/bindings/cros_flash/cros-ec,flash-layout.yaml",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 50,
      "author": {
        "id": 1478788
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-29T19:51:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it make sense trying to change the binman default value? Padding something that ends in flash with 0 by default still sounds off.",
      "parentUuid": "8069c526_594b5971",
      "revId": "8e86c7b0aa8c2afed21d9a9632b615682987d824",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
